<title>BRAZIL: Glencore Brazil say U.S. soybean sale fell through.</title>
<headline>Glencore Brazil say U.S. soybean sale fell through.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A trader at Glencore in Brazil said that a 45,000 tonne sale of soybeans to a U.S. firm which he earlier confirmed had fallen through and did not actually occur.</p>
<p>&quot;It ended up not being done,&quot; the trader said. &quot;We had everything all set up and were about to do it but in the end it didn't work out.&quot;</p>
<p>The trader on Wednesday confirmed market talk that Glencore had sold 45,00 tonnes of Brazilian soybeans to a U.S. firm, which contributed to a tumble in soybean futures prices in Chicago.  </p>
<p>The trader added that Glencore now had no soybean or soymeal sales on the books for the U.S.. &quot;Here, we have nothing,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
